From 6bcbba80971dcd069fb48abd0664f826f08b1ef0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juanan <juanan@test.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:18:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] T3: add academic validation with history

- A grade can be validated once by a user with
  gradingform/rubric_ranges:validate who is not its grader. The validator
  grade and feedback replace the teacher ones; the original teacher grade,
  level, feedback and grader are kept in gradingform_rubric_ranges_h
  (validation_history persistent) with the validator and the date.
- validation_manager decides one state per user and grade (off, normal,
  validated, not graded, self, pending) used both to render and to save.
- Locked submissions are ignored on the server and keep the current grade;
  the submitter copy of the grading instance is discarded so the
  validator never becomes the grader. Validated grades are read only.
- Site admins are not validators unless a role grants the capability.
- "Validate" button (AMD validation) swaps the read only teacher rubric
  for the editable one. Graders see who validated and the original grade;
  students do not see the validation.
- New event grade_validated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
